{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Now let me die this time.</b> For before this, his life had been a life of suffering, and he was reckoned as dead during his lifetime, as though he were already dead and had passed and vanished from the world. But now that it was said, ״וַתְּחִי רוּחַ יַעֲקֹב אֲבִיהֶם״ (Genesis 45:27) — that he became a living man again — from now on he would be destined for death only once and not many deaths. For one who is reckoned as dead on account of a life of suffering is as though he dies every single day. And so too it is said, ״וַיְחִי יַעֲקֹב בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם שְׁבַע עֶשְׂרֵה שָׁנָה וַיְהִי יְמֵי יַעֲקֹב שְׁנֵי חַיָּיו שֶׁבַע שָׁנִים וְאַרְבָּעִים וּמְאַת שָׁנָה״ (Genesis 47:28), for by virtue of the life of tranquility that he had during those seventeen years, it was retroactively as though he had lived all one hundred and forty-seven years a pleasant life that is called life in truth."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:40.284877083Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}